# Engines pin these files by SHA-256 of their exact bytes, so every checkout,
# on every platform, must keep LF line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ppm binary
*.pgm binary
*.pfm binary

# Files pinned by a SHA-256 list: SHA256SUMS pins the three implementations,
# examples/reference/raw-native-0.4.0/SHA256SUMS pins the recorded reference, and
# vectors/MANIFEST.json pins every vector. `eol=lf` above writes LF on checkout, but
# Git still converts these files on commit and checkout. `-text` turns conversion
# off for exactly these paths, so the bytes on disk are the committed blob under any
# core.autocrlf setting. Later lines win, so this overrides the rule above here only.
/SHA256SUMS -text
/superstack.py -text
/superstack.mjs -text
/superstack.hpp -text
examples/reference/raw-native-0.4.0/SHA256SUMS -text
examples/reference/raw-native-0.4.0/certificate.json -text
vectors/*.json -text
